Login endpoint-ku stricter rate limit use pannalaam.

Create middleware/loginLimiter.js:
const rateLimit = require("express-rate-limit");

const loginLimiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,
  limit: 5,
  message: {
    message: "Too many login attempts. Try again later."
  },
  standardHeaders: "draft-8",
  legacyHeaders: false
});

module.exports = loginLimiter;


Use it in your login route:
const loginLimiter = require("./middleware/loginLimiter");

app.use("/api/auth/login", loginLimiter);


Interview point: Login rate limiting helps reduce brute-force password attacks. Production systems may also use account-based throttling and monitoring.
